  "finalText": "I made no changes. The R8116 over-refund is real, but I can't undo it with the tools I have.\n\n**Current state of R8116:**\n- **L5:** a 12000 baggage fee. The correct fee for a silver economy passenger with 3 bags is 4500, so the overcharge is 7500. It is annotated \"overcharged\", which is correct.\n- **L24:** a 2000 courtesy refund of L5 to the original payment method, posted by agent-3 on 2026-07-27, before the audit.\n- **L26:** a 7500 travel credit that I issued as the audit settlement.\n- **Total returned:** 9500 against a 7500 overcharge, so the customer is 2000 over-refunded. The audit should have issued only 5500.\n\n**Why I'm not fixing it:**\n- No tool reduces or reverses a refund or travel-credit entry. `refund_fee` and `issue_refund` only send money out, so I can't cut L26 from 7500 to 5500.\n- Charging a 2000 fee to claw the money back would be re-billing, and the handbook rules out re-billing on fee audits.\n- There is also no payment instrument on file for R8116, so there is nothing to recover the money from.\n\nI'm not treating the issue as mistaken. It is accurate, but I can't act on the correction. Whoever owns credit adjustments needs to reduce L26 to 5500 or write off the 2000. I have not messaged the customer, because a message now would add confusion without fixing anything.",
